  "subject": "science",
  "summary": "A semester of kindergarten science about weather: watching the sky every day, dressing for the weather, sun and shade, wind, rain and water, the four seasons, and staying safe in any weather. Seven units, each with a read-aloud overview for students, a teacher guide with a five-day plan, a lesson, assignments, an assessment with a rubric and an answer key. Built around the kindergarten weather and climate ideas in science; aligned to kindergarten Common Core speaking, writing and counting standards that students use to record and talk about the weather.",
  "title": "Kindergarten Science: Weather Watchers",
